      "body": "Adds a Windows Chrome 156 profile with the version-seeded Client Hints brand order, a navigation Accept header including image/jxl, sorted trust anchors, and an explicit zero-byte server-padding request.\n\nDepends on https://github.com/0x676e67/wreq/pull/1362. The wreq git patch temporarily points to that PR head so this branch can compile before its API is released; it must be updated to the accepted upstream revision before merging.\n\nThe profile targets the initial TLS/HTTP2 configuration observed with Windows Chrome for Testing 156.0.8078.73. Server padding is experimental and configuration-dependent. Chrome for Testing uses Chromium branding; the Google Chrome brand list is derived from Chromium's version-seeded ordering. Other platforms, resumed sessions, HTTP3, and complete browser equivalence are not validated.\n\nExtends the trust-anchor checks and adds loopback ClientHello tests for extension 4832 (payload 0000), covering client-wide/per-request emulation and fresh connections. The Chrome154 control omits that extension. Existing profiles are unchanged.\n\nFormatting and diff checks pass. An equivalent native consumer profile has compiled and emitted the expected extension. Repository Cargo tests are delegated to CI because the available local Rust 1.94.1 is below the required 1.98.",
